"endLine":224,"endLineOffset":5,"length":589}]}]},{"comment":"The change in `#8PJ1J` replaces `UnsupportedAttribute` with `UnresolvedAttribute`. This change is consistent with the new method introduced in `#ETZGN`, which now includes an additional parameter `allowUnionTypes`. However, the usage of `UnresolvedAttribute` without specifying a qualifier and unresolved message might lead to confusion or incorrect behavior if these fields are expected elsewhere in the codebase. Ensure that the absence of these parameters does not cause issues downstream.\nThe new method `isType` introduced in `#ETZGN` includes an additional parameter `allowUnionTypes`. This change is significant and should be reviewed to ensure that all call sites are updated appropriately, especially since some callsites still use the old method signature (e.g., `#FS04S`). The TODO comment about widening small numerical types suggests that there might be further work needed in this area.\nThe change in `#MCEDF` updates the call to `isType` by adding the `allowUnionTypes` parameter. This is consistent with the changes made in `#ETZGN`. However, it\u0027s important to verify that setting `allowUnionTypes` to `true` does not introduce any unintended behavior or security issues.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql-core/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/core/expression/TypeResolutions.java-x-pack/plugin/esql-core/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/core/expression/TypeResolutions.java-6817:7403-6883:6958","promptId":"#FS04S","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql-core/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/core/expression/TypeResolutions.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql-core/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/core/expression/TypeResolutions.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":6817,"endPos":7403,"startLine":179,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":191,"endLineOffset":14,"length":587}],"dstChanges":[{"pos":6883,"endPos":6958,"startLine":180,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":180,"endLineOffset":83,"length":76}